{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement","id":1513370,"title":"You are tasked as the architect of a great vampire settlement.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-31T04:02:21-07:00","id":1513370,"title":"You are tasked as the architect of a great vampire settlement.","content":"Think a bunker or a hidden city in the middle of nowhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible clients include: </b><br /> -Someone who believes Gehenna or some other apocalyptic event is nigh.<br /> -someone with extreme isolationist tendencies or who wants to escape the Jyhad.<br /> -A former king who misses being a king (bonus points if you can put in a castle) or someone overly enthusiastic about their interpretation of the second city.<br /> -A billionaire narcissist with delusions of granduer <i>(I'm not sure about the possibilities when utilizing awakened magicks but mundane-wise living on Mars is too much of a stretch, but if Vampires went to the moon would their sleep cycles be moon time? That might be more convenient) </i><br /> <br /> -A Ventrue has very specific but-endangered tastes and will go to extreme measures to protect his herd. A malkavian with compulsively extreme protectiveness over her herd wants a safe space.<br /> -A Tzmisce wants a controlled environment for his experiments ,<br /> - An infernalist or some kind of cultist who wants to do this to please his demon/god master<br /> <br /> <b>Client concerns:</b><br /> -It needs to be built with secrecy, but a lot of manpower will be needed for the build: the place needs to be large with many facilities so nobody gets bored or overly suicidal and the human population needs to be large enough to prevent inbreeding. Keeping such a large project secret will be a massive undertaking.<br /> -The human population need to be well fed with a variety of food, and this needs to be done secretly.<br /> -The humans can't escape to tell the world.<br /> <br /> Where do you build it, how do you build it, what measures do you take to keep the people in, what Disciplines or other powers do you need to maintain control? What kind of hooks could you put in that draw the players into finding the settlement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-31-2023, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T05:28:24-07:00","id":1513377,"title":"","content":"I love these!<br /> My obvious sulution would be an underground city, either literally underground, or inside a mountian<br /> Earth have lots of underground water suplies, whole seas under the surface, the logical soultion would be building around one of those. Lake Martel is in Drach Caves (Cuevas del Drach), located on the southeastern coast of Mallorca, in Porto Cristo, it is the biggest underground lake in the world, 117 metres long, 30 metres wide and between 4 and 12 metres deep. But the Drach Caves have several. The largest Underground Lakes in the World are Krizna Cave Lake in Slovenia, Son Doong Cave in Vietnam, the Owey Island Lake in Ireland, Grj\u00f3tagj\u00e1 in Iceland, the Lost Sea in Tennessee, USA just to name a few.<br /> Eithert use a pre-existing one or find a bit smaller, less known<br /> Now the logical qustion, how long can you live without exposure to sunlight?<br /> The answer: normal lifespan, with the right diet. Recent research suggests that sunlight deprivation might increase susceptibility to a wide range of chronic diseases, such as diabetes and high blood pressure, as well as infectious diseases such as tuberculosis and the common cold, but it's very unlikely an adult could die directly and exclusively from prolonged darkness. The most plausible deadly scenario is that a lack of sunlight could prevent the body from producing vitamin D, which, in turn, would inhibit calcium absorption. Very low calcium levels might lead to spasms of the larynx, causing suffocation. A proper diet, however, can easily stave off this unlikely chain of events and other health consequences, even if you live in a bunker. Vitamin D is present in egg yolks, cheese, fatty fish, and fortified milk, juice and cereal.<br /> Mushroom, fungi and moss (and lichen even) - or since we are with a lake, fish and algae and seaweed are a good basis to sustain a balanced diet, even could introduce cave dwelling reptiles, fishes, bugs in the diet, and of course goats and cows and pigs <br /> The later ones are good source of methane (Mad Max 3 stlye) to heat, and generate eletricity<br /> In a nice big cave, you even could have your own castle in the middle<br /> Think about the Drow cities<br /> As for population... according the studies to remain genetically flexible and diverse \u2013 the IUCN criteria suggest - we would need at least 500 effective individuals - but studies also show, the bare minimum to avoid any complication is just 98 people<br /> I would start by... well, kidnapping kids. Or homeless Or homeless kids.<br /> Terrible as it may sound, no one would look for them. They are nonexistant in the eyes of the community<br /> With young enough could be easly conitioned to not even know the modern world - or gather your population from already backwater areas, even in the 21st century, there are plenty<br /> And keep the population around stone age or bronze age level - or if you are generous, gather doomsday preps, who already have plans to live such conditions to survive anything, dealers choice basically<br /> In your Citadell, hoard the knowledge, technology, and time to time train a few smart bright human to keep on eye of the machinery if you have any<br /> The beauty of a not so advanced society, you don't really need huge projects to prepare all of this;a few fungual farms, animals, and your dream dark ages village in the darkness will flourish<br /> If you want your humans to actually see (eventually they will adapt, just give them a few generation) use.. .well anything that produce bioluminescence; fungi, mushrooms, glow worm, firefly, dinoflagellates... there are plenty<br /> But if you want it large and advanced... well it is the same, just large and advanced, could intorduce eletricty via generators run on the said methane (or even geothermal energy) or compost and once you have energy, technology is not an issue. \u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T05:33:23-07:00","id":1513379,"title":"","content":"If you google &quot;billionaire bunkers&quot; you will get plenty of resources (including schematics) for the real life industry centered around catering to very rich doomsday preppers; there should be enough overlap for a starting point. This includes questions on how to handle a large number of slaves that cater to the needs of their master. Yes, people professionally discuss questions wether electric collars are a good way to ensure the loyalty of the plebs enshrined with their tyrant.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it should provide a basic infrastructure. Few actual locations are public of course, but since most of the bunkers are repurposed military structures they tend to be in isolated areas like deserts or steppes. Large plains also have the benefit of making aerial supply possible, initially at least, and provide a natural border that prevents escape. Using or expanding an already established structure also helps with secrecy. I would say that eliminating information about a location is easier than trying to build a large structure without anyone noticing (in the satellite era). Regardless of whether you build in Antarctica or on Mars, some eye in the sky is going to mark it down.<br /> Actually, while a logistic nightmare, moving the operation into a different realm might be the safest bet. Enoch manged to go on for a pretty long while. Lorewise there is also Alamut for an isolated enclave, but the Assamite Clanbook wastes little space on the specifics of the involved logistics iirc.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem for doomsday bunkers is that no-one has managed to create a sustainable isolated biosphere yet. Surface agriculture is both a risk of exposure and to security, so going full underground would be the clearly preferred option- luckily, blood magic (or straight up Magick) provides ways to cheat away the problem of how to feed the mortal Herd. Still neither easy nor inexpensive, but at least possible. If you go with the Enoch option, you may be able to minimize the required effort, depending on the rules of the realm. The Bahari somehow found a way to support a mortal populace in the underworld, of all places. If figure the middle umbra might be more accommodating.<br /> <br /> I guess the question about specific Disciplines (magic always helps) and possible hooks hinges on the location and type, but in general, any &quot;Lost City&quot; style hooks would do. Picking up a paper trail, rumors, etc.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you're interested, the Earthdawn RPG has this very scenario as an essential back-story element; One city, Parlainth, decided to nope out of dimension instead of bunkering down. It did not end well, but has some very entertaining setting novels as result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 05-31-2023, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T05:46:30-07:00","id":1513381,"title":"","content":"<s>Use vicissitude and build myself a house in the middle of nowhere, alone, using the clients' bodies as the materials.</s><br /> <br /> So then, crazy and probably unworkable ideas:<br /> <br /> Location: As close to the poles as possible, possibly on them. Antarctica looks nice. While this means that half the year the vampire populace will be non-functioning, for the other half of the year you have a lot of activity time. It also provides isolation and adorable pet ghoul penguins. The only downside is that you won't be readily available half the year to keep an eye on things.<br /> There's plenty of empty territory to go around, so rather than a shared settlement, everyone can take over or establish their own research base or ice castle or something. What you do there is your own business. Except for the infernalist, he sounds like trouble and we should all throw him in the volcano for our own good.<br /> If it must be a joint location, I believe there are ice caves that look quite pleasant and wouldn't turn up on google maps.<br /> <br /> Learning fortitude and protean may be necessary for all inhabitants who wish to avoid frostbite and navigate their surroundings. Thaumaturgy will be invaluable. Maybe levinbolt, technomancy and conjuring can substitute for manufacturing and provide electricity, security and other modern conveniences. A combination of lure of flames and neptune's might could be used for reshaping ice into structures, perhaps? Dominate, chimestry and presence can be employed to keep the inhabitants, kindred and kine - happy, well behaved and occupied. If you can find a way to manipulate the nearby volcanoes (maybe with the way of fire or something) you might be able to get geothermal heating.<br /> <br /> The lack of civilisation means that, in case of Gehenna, there are unlikely to be any ancients in the area, nor will the area be of much interest to rivals.<br /> The defenses will include ghouled orcas on patrol around the continent because making the already sadistic murder dolphins high on the essence of murder sounds darkly hilarious.<br /> <br /> Food:<br /> The massive downside here is keeping the kine alive, it is definitely not suitable for the human species and bunkers may be hard to maintain, as well as the food requirements. Ghouling them would require vitae. Revenants may be hardier (and longer lived to boot), but may be hard to get enough of them to keep a stable population for feeding. Perhaps enough uses of vicissitude combining traits of the cold-resistant local fauna with humans could do something to stop the humans dying from frostbite?<br /> <br /> And no amount of ghouling will help with the fact that the herds need a food supply. Can plants be ghouled? Two dots in the green path might help, since we would not be at the mercy of time to get edible crops. Speed the Season's Passing, being magic, possibly does away with the requirement for fertile soil. Grab a potato, magic it, get about ten potatoes. Repeat. Job done. (Honestly, the usurpers have been sleeping on the untapped potential of agricultural rituals.)<br /> Unless you find a way to make them cold resistant, vampires may need to hunt and fish for their herds themselves. Or pay a gangrel to do it. Or train animal ghouls to do it.<br /> <br /> How much blood do whales have, for feeding purposes?<br /> <br /> Antarctica does get tourists and military and researchers who come and go, if some of them go missing now and then and happen to end up in the herds, well, it's a harsh environment. You can also feed on the research bases rather than an established herd from time to time, and if they say anything they'll make terrible witnesses considering scientists stationed at these places tend to go loopy anyway. And kine that escape the herd will die on the ice long before they find anyone to tell.<br /> <br /> Edit: Alternative feeding method: take a thinblood (who cannot form bonds), fleshcraft it so that it has no senses or limbs and is nothing more than a fleshy sack with a hole you can pour blood into. Pour animal blood in, bleed vitae out. Serve to the local population.<br /> Keep a thinblood larder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-31-2023, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T07:07:13-07:00","id":1513391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513381#post1513381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can plants be ghouled?</div> </div> </div> </div>While straight up plant ghouls aren't a thing, there are numerous instances of 'effects' vitae has on plant life, such as specific rituals and Disciplines/Paths (Ogham, Green Path, Sielanic Thauma, and I think some Bahari Paths in the Tal'mahe'ra book), but also more narrative ones like grotesque gardens and such. Could make for an interesting experiment in indirect ghouling and keeping tabs on the populace, actually. Probably expensive in blood though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T07:45:32-07:00","id":1513393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513381#post1513381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can plants be ghouled?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mexico City by Night describes <b>Caridad de Flores </b>and her quite deadly garden and plants<br /> The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra mentions, only normally carnivore plants are ghoulable with <i>normal methods - </i>emphasis on normal. So basically, ST descrition like everything; just find a not really normal method <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T07:59:59-07:00","id":1513395,"title":"","content":"I was mostly thinking about how to teach crops fortitude and give them vampiric regeneration powers to make them more likely to survive, but all that's interesting to know and will be useful to me. Could also borrow the mandragora from Requiem (ghouled plants whose sap turns to a vitae-like substance that vampires can eat... and get drunk on.)<br /> <br /> And while I'm not good enough at understanding this part of the setting to really iron it out, I have occasionally wondered about founding an open vampire society somewhere in the Umbra. Is that more or less untenable than vampire space colonies, I wonder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:29:07-07:00","id":1513419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513393#post1513393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mexico City by Night describes <b>Caridad de Flores </b>and her quite deadly garden and plants<br /> The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra mentions, only normally carnivore plants are ghoulable with <i>normal methods - </i>emphasis on normal. So basically, ST descrition like everything; just find a not really normal method <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected, apparently the Rafastio had some limited success in actually ghouling plants. I'm not sure how viable teaching a discipline to a plant would be, I can't imagine they are very good pupils. I can't deny Audrey II had some Presence to her, though.<br /> <br /> There's a Vicissitude power in the book that allows indirect ghouling via pouring vitae into plant soil, so at least that's possible in some fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:42:30-07:00","id":1513422,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Green path would be much good, since it's a one-plant thing. Maybe for fruit trees, but for crops? no. The blood you put in wouldn't match the returns for a lot of things. IDK maybe people can do really well with a vampire taking blood and getting mangoes, pears and bannanas in return. But, fruits are like, reproductive organs or somethingsuch, so like will speeding things up actually enable fertilization and the growth of fruit? If you had the power to speed up a woman's growth will she somehow get pregnant on her own? I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T11:15:13-07:00","id":1513427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513422#post1513422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Green path would be much good, since it's a one-plant thing. Maybe for fruit trees, but for crops? no. The blood you put in wouldn't match the returns for a lot of things. IDK maybe people can do really well with a vampire taking blood and getting mangoes, pears and bannanas in return. But, fruits are like, reproductive organs or somethingsuch, so like will speeding things up actually enable fertilization and the growth of fruit? If you had the power to speed up a woman's growth will she somehow get pregnant on her own? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ghoul pollinators and keep an apiary or something, maybe? (I wonder if vitae might have an effect on honey)<br /> &quot;Engineer&quot; your own insects with sorcery and/or vicissitude?<br /> Use a paint brush and pollinate the flowers manually? If you've got blood to spare you can speed it up to make it bloom, pollinate it, and then speed it up again to get food.<br /> <br /> Also, can the path of conjuration make soil? At the very least, it can probably make planters, insulation and grow lights, so greenhouses might be possible. Can power over life make plants? Hands of Destruction can maybe get you compost on demand...<br /> <br /> ...How many dots of vicissitude do you need to alter humans to be able to live on a strictly carnivorous diet anyway?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T11:37:12-07:00","id":1513429,"title":"","content":"The restrictions of the path of alchemy should be assumed to apply to Conjuration: you can't really create &quot;reactive&quot; elements or anything that changes state, so eating something you conjured isn't going to be nutritious.<br /> <br /> Hand of destruction.. it's single target right? Do you think it can be used on an area? Is it worth using because things rot kind of quickly<br /> <br /> I don't really know about soil quality or how to put nutrients into hydroponics, but power is kind of easy and you can grow things with artificial light and I think getting water isn't something terribly difficult underground. You just need enough space, and space is difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-31-2023, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:15:02-07:00","id":1513434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513422#post1513422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Green path would be much good, since it's a one-plant thing. Maybe for fruit trees, but for crops? no. The blood you put in wouldn't match the returns for a lot of things. IDK maybe people can do really well with a vampire taking blood and getting mangoes, pears and bannanas in return. But, fruits are like, reproductive organs or somethingsuch, so like will speeding things up actually enable fertilization and the growth of fruit? If you had the power to speed up a woman's growth will she somehow get pregnant on her own? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything fertility related is usually outside the scope of Vampires (if you don't count making people horny), and it should be. Outsource, go oldschool and use Spirit Manipulation. Pampering a spirit into extended service for good crops and husbandry is probably the most cost effective method, and I imagine one of the most common things the Path was used for in the Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:15:10-07:00","id":1513435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513429#post1513429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just need enough space, and space is difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hire a Kaisyd who knows the old Mytherceria power Goblinism who thus not only would have Intuitive direction sense underground but would be able to summon goblins to help him to warp and reshape stone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:20:41-07:00","id":1513436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513434#post1513434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything fertility related is usually outside the scope of Vampires (if you don't count making people horny), and it should be. .</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a nice level 1 Akhu ritual called <b>Seal the Gates of Blood - </b>The Setite crafts a small amulet that has to be worn by a woman. A woman who wears the amulet will not miscarry, and her menses are greatly reduced. Menstrual blood, however, is directly passed into the blood pool of the Setite who crafted the amulet.<br /> <br /> Not quite fertility relatd, but making sure a woman will not miscarry? Imho insanely usefull and powerfull thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:37:41-07:00","id":1513440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513429#post1513429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand of destruction.. it's single target right? Do you think it can be used on an area? Is it worth using because things rot kind of quickly<br /> <br /> I don't really know about soil quality or how to put nutrients into hydroponics, but power is kind of easy and you can grow things with artificial light and I think getting water isn't something terribly difficult underground. You just need enough space, and space is difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decay appears to be single target. So if you use it on a large chunk of bedrock or dig into an ice sheet you might be able to use it this way? From sufficiently broken down rock you might be able to get planting material, and then you can break down organic matter, which makes it ideal for gardening afterwards. <br /> The rest of the path is no use.<br /> <br /> Gnarl Wood can explicitly target multiple objects, up to 25kg per blood point, but it only affects wood.<br /> <br /> Acidic Touch: One blood point creates enough acid to<br /> burn through a quarter-inch or half a centimeter of steel<br /> plate or three inches (seven centimeters) of wood.<br /> Not much use without mass sacrifice.<br /> <br /> The remaining dots all target people.<br /> <br /> Maybe alchemy? I think an older version of the path enabled shifting states, so you could use it to fiddle with the chemical makeup and get rid of most if a mass by turning some of it into gas and then flushing it out? <br /> <br /> I guess you could also just send in workers armed with potence and celerity to simply excavate it manually. That leaves the question of what to do with the leftover mass. I guess if there are any necromancers around you could use the Ash Path to open a door to the Dark Umbra, dump it on the other side and make it the underworld's problem? (I don't think there are any necropoli or anything of interest in Shadowland Antarctica, so it shouldn't be an issue.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:40:29-07:00","id":1513466,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to get a bunker is to simply buy a decommissioned cold war bunker/installation and retrofit it to vampiric needs. In the US you can buy nuclear missile silos for only about $350,000 and it takes less than $500,000 more to retrofit it to modern standards. That is still less than the cost of a lot of California houses on the market. Presumably anywhere else in the world that had American or Russian installations should have similar options.<br /> <br /> A setup like the converted underground silo can house up to about 75 people for about 5 years without having to resupply. Figure that each silo would house one coterie with the remaining 65-70 people being a communal Herd or personal ghoul servants. Given how little vampires need to survive, and how much they could curtail the living standards of the mortals, you could probably stretch that out to 8 years without needing a resupply. If you cut the number of mortals down and give over the unused space to more food generation, you could probably stay down they quite a while longer.<br /> <br /> The logical extension of this line of thinking is to create a &quot;company town&quot; in the middle of a very harsh environment. You see this a lot in Russia where cities won't have names, just number designations and they will be hundreds of miles from the nearest settlement. Access to the city is accomplished by railroad or local airport. What you do is build an entire subterranean vampire city, and then build the mortal city on top. The city itself is more or less self-contained and the vampire city keeps isolated underground. The key benefit of this is that the vampire section is purpose built rather than being retrofitted to existing human sewer systems.<br /> <br /> In either case the resident vampires will need a smattering of different clans/bloodlines to increase their chances of survival. Tremere invaluable for being able to setup Wards and use Paths to act as emergency stop gap measures. The Path of Conjuring more or less can create any chemical, machined part, or basic tool you need. As others have mentioned the Green Path makes establishing food tree orchards ridiculously easy. Having some sort of Necromancer bloodline or clan present would advisable since Ghosts will probably be plentiful in a post Gehenna world and not many people or creatures can counter them. Lastly some Gangrel would be excellent as scouts and animal tamers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T22:55:34-07:00","id":1513606,"title":"","content":"Where: Pick one of these. <a href=\"https://largest.org/people/uninhabited-islands/\" target=\"_blank\">https://largest.org/people/uninhabited-islands/</a><br /> How to keep them in: It's an Island where would they go?<br /> Disciplines needed: Depends on choice, but Dominate with Protean in harsh environments Maybe high Thaumaturgy to have some sort of cloaking ritual vs spy satellites and something to scramble communications near the Island.<br /> Adventure hooks: Rumors of an ancient text being hidden there? It's about 2am, too tired to think it through...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T10:39:42-07:00","id":1513667,"title":"","content":"An Island is probably too difficult to supply/build facilities on, I mean if you try really hard you can probably do it but keeping such a big logistical undertaking a secret is way too difficult. Most uninhabited islands are uninhabited for a reason. <br /> Building a billionaire bunker of the scale needed seems too much to keep secret I think. In most cases, other vampires are a concern. <br /> I like the company town idea. How would you keep the construction crew quiet though? Making ghost towns from real estate bubbles is all cool and normal but making undercities is bound to arouse interest. <br /> <br /> Trying to look things up, and I may be wrong<br /> To keep a human fed using the best human technology you need like 1200m2, roughly the size of an Olympic swimming pool. I don't know how capable we are of layering those farms on top of one another. Presumably best human technology also means some fertilizers/pesticides are needed. In more forgiving scenarios, you could perhaps farm on the surface and with a big enough farm excuse the missing food, though you may have to deal with suspicious inmates questioning where the food is coming from, but the worst case IE we need to do everything underground is really the best thing to plan for I think. <br /> You need at least 500 animals in a population to prevent inbreeding issues in nature. Not sure how selective programs would change this number","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T11:56:55-07:00","id":1513674,"title":"","content":"One thing that occurred to me, depending on how willing you are to stretch the definition of 'Haven' for any large complex like this, the usually somewhat mediocre Hearth Path becomes really useful. Same for Visceratika powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T19:28:58-07:00","id":1513738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513466#post1513466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The logical extension of this line of thinking is to create a &quot;company town&quot; in the middle of a very harsh environment. You see this a lot in Russia where cities won't have names, just number designations and they will be hundreds of miles from the nearest settlement. Access to the city is accomplished by railroad or local airport. What you do is build an entire subterranean vampire city, and then build the mortal city on top. The city itself is more or less self-contained and the vampire city keeps isolated underground. The key benefit of this is that the vampire section is purpose built rather than being retrofitted to existing human sewer systems.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Doethe mundane or normal section or emoloyees of the government receive help, news, support, trust,, and respect from the local and normal government or some help and support service ?<br /> Could you say more about the Vampires that would be creating and organizing this place ? What would be their particular values, goals, ambitions, and objectives ?<br /> Having an extensive dungeons and caves systems and sections is certainly a good approach to location planning and city building. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T18:59:32-07:00","id":1513839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513370-you-are-tasked-as-the-architect-of-a-great-vampire-settlement?p=1513738#post1513738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doethe mundane or normal section or emoloyees of the government receive help, news, support, trust,, and respect from the local and normal government or some help and support service ?<br /> Could you say more about the Vampires that would be creating and organizing this place ? What would be their particular values, goals, ambitions, and objectives ?<br /> Having an extensive dungeons and caves systems and sections is certainly a good approach to location planning and city building.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL the russian cities were usually research or refining locations for tech or war critical infrastructure. So the residents would have a &quot;higher&quot; standard of living than most civilians, but they were all living around uranium enrichment labs, bio weapons labs, Area 51 type of testing areas, etc. This provided a great deal of security with an easily controlled population. Then Satellites became a thing and then became less useful. Obviously there is a give and take between the cities and the government in terms of supplies shipped in and production output.<br /> <br /> In the case of a vampire version of this setup I could see a surface city that is located in a Desert location like the Mojave or the Sahara. The above ground city would be built as a test design for solar and wind power development on a city scale built from the ground up, rather than trying to add such things to older city designs. Depending how far away the next city is, the company town could sell excess power back to the local grid, function as a data center location, or just hand wave &quot;research&quot; place like the hive in Raccoon City. Really you can mix and match the above and below ground infrastructure for some really interesting storyline fodder.<br /> <br /> As for the design of the underground section of the city, that really depends on the clans involved and their relationship to humans. I have played around with several version of this. <br /> <br /> I did one version where the entire underground section is a unified city run by a vampire council, but while each clan is represented, the factions such as Camarilla, Sabbat, Innocu are more akin to political parties. Which means while there is loads of political infighting, it is more deal making and less besieging new territory. This version works well in the last civilized city in the world scenario or with a contemporary setting but the shifters and other dangerous supernaturals are constantly laying siege.<br /> <br /> Another version is that rather than having a single city per se, the city has a several smaller warrens/hives. I used the diagram of the underground missile silo doomsday condos as a baseline for each area. This way each clan had its own territory, had its own live in herd, and had its own rules. The above ground city more or less hid the location and provided a supply of potential embrace and herd membership.<br /> <br /> A third version of the underground vampire city I did turned everything on its head. The above ground city was a very remote jungle or mountain town with subsistence level agriculture or herding. The vampires built a stone age tech level undercity, they were all on Gangrel and on the path of Feral Heart or Path of Harmony. Basically the mortal city and surrounding area was the Gangrels private hunting grounds. They hunted and killed the mortals that caused damage to the area or the city, while harmlessly feeding from the well behaved mortals while they slept. The Gangrel specifically brought mortals to this hidden place to build this society, kind of like how Lunar Exalted build their own pet hobby societies. When the end of the world comes, not much would change with this sort of setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}